    {
      "id": "cp_mrs_pwr",
      "gender": "Female",
      "hasShell": false,
      "partNumber": "90980-12068",
      "description": "MR-S EHPS pump — main power connector housing (pigtail 82998-12500). Toyota generic connector family (Sumitomo TS090 / Yazaki 090-II series) - NOT a TE Connectivity part (checked TE's site, no match; this is Toyota/Sumitomo). Pin 1 = switched 12V in from relay 87, pin 2 = ground. Confirmed against Daniel's photos of the pump (DIY Electric Car Forums 'MR2 Gen3 Power Steering Help' diagram, connector 'A'). Part number sourced from a separate DIYElectricCar thread ('Power Steering using Toyota MR2 EHPS pump') - cross-check against the pump in hand before ordering. - OWNED (Daniel confirmed on hand)",
      "manufacturer": "Toyota",
      "configurations": [
        {
          "id": "cfg",
          "contactPartId": "ct_toy_ts"
        }
      ],
      "numberOfCavities": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "cp_mrs_en",
      "gender": "Female",
      "hasShell": false,
      "partNumber": "90980-10942",
      "description": "MR-S EHPS pump — small ignition-enable connector housing (pigtail 82998-12440, shared with the control connector). Toyota generic connector family (Sumitomo TS090 / Yazaki 090-II series) - NOT a TE Connectivity part. 2 cavities, only pin 1 used (ignition-switched 12V logic supply); pin 2 unused. Confirmed against Daniel's photos of the pump (DIY Electric Car Forums 'MR2 Gen3 Power Steering Help' diagram, connector 'C'). Part number sourced from a separate DIYElectricCar thread ('Power Steering using Toyota MR2 EHPS pump') - cross-check against the pump in hand before ordering. - OWNED (Daniel confirmed on hand)",
      "manufacturer": "Toyota",
      "configurations": [
        {
          "id": "cfg",
          "contactPartId": "ct_toy_ts"
        }
      ],
      "numberOfCavities": 2
    }
  ],
